IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tar-core`

-- Transport Accident Regulations 2017 (Vic) -- from the seat of the individual the Regulations are applied to.
--
-- SEAT: the person injured in a transport accident (is my injury a severe injury; how much can be paid for modifying
-- my home without an agreement); the person receiving weekly payments for loss of earning capacity (my statement of
-- earnings); the driver, owner or owner's parent asked by the Commission to report an accident; and the owner of a
-- trailer, or the person in charge of it, insured under the contract in Form 4. Each question is phrased as that
-- person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in tar-core.l4; this module turns plain
-- answers into the core's inputs and restates no rule.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transport Accident Regulations 2017 (Vic) -- the individual's questions`

§§ `Is my injury a severe injury (Act s 3(1); r 5)`

-- Builds the core's record from plain answers.
GIVEN `h` IS A `Head of s 3(1)(a) other than burns`, `pct` IS A NUMBER, `dis` IS A BOOLEAN, `ftb` IS A BOOLEAN
      `mob` IS A BOOLEAN, `com` IS A BOOLEAN, `sc` IS A BOOLEAN, `fld` IS A NUMBER, `ra` IS A NUMBER, `la` IS A NUMBER
      `comb` IS A BOOLEAN, `bp` IS A BOOLEAN, `limb` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Injury facts`
`my injury` `h` `pct` `dis` `ftb` `mob` `com` `sc` `fld` `ra` `la` `comb` `bp` `limb` MEANS
    `Injury facts` WITH
        `the other s 3(1)(a) head`                         IS `h`
        `the percentage of the body burned`                IS `pct`
        `severe disfigurement`                             IS `dis`
        `full-thickness burns to the head, neck, arms or lower legs` IS `ftb`
        `severe difficulty with mobility tasks`            IS `mob`
        `severe difficulty with communication tasks`       IS `com`
        `severe difficulty with self-care tasks`           IS `sc`
        `the field of vision of the better eye`            IS `fld`
        `the right eye's corrected acuity`                 IS `ra`
        `the left eye's corrected acuity`                  IS `la`
        `a combination of defects gives the same loss`     IS `comb`
        `a brachial plexus injury`                         IS `bp`
        `the loss of the use of a limb from it`            IS `limb`

@export Is my transport accident injury a severe injury under the Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) s 3(1) and the Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 5? A severe injury opens the safety net income benefit (s 54A), home services without the 5-year limit (s 60(2AC)), family counselling (s 60(2A)(a)), travel allowance and individual funding agreements (ss 60B, 61A) and the supported employment rule (s 49(9)). The definition does not apply in Part 6 (common law damages).
GIVEN `my injury is` IS A `Head of s 3(1)(a) other than burns` @desc Is your injury a significant acquired brain injury, paraplegia, quadriplegia or the amputation of a limb? Choose none of these if not.
      `the percentage of my body burned` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of your body was burned (0 if none)?
      `my burns cause severe disfigurement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your burns cause severe disfigurement?
      `I have full-thickness burns to my head, neck, arms or lower legs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your burns include full-thickness burns to your head, neck, arms or lower legs?
      `my full-thickness burns severely hinder mobility tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your full-thickness burns cause severe difficulties in performing mobility tasks?
      `my full-thickness burns severely hinder communication tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your full-thickness burns cause severe difficulties in performing communication tasks?
      `my full-thickness burns severely hinder self-care tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your full-thickness burns cause severe difficulties in performing self-care tasks?
      `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many degrees of arc from central fixation is the field of vision of your better eye constricted (enter 90 if your field of vision is not affected)?
      `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the corrected visual acuity of your right eye on the Snellen scale, as a number (6/6 is 1, 6/60 is 0.1, 3/60 is 0.05)?
      `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the corrected visual acuity of your left eye on the Snellen scale, as a number (6/6 is 1, 6/60 is 0.1, 3/60 is 0.05)?
      `my combined visual defects equal that loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been assessed that a combination of your visual defects gives the same degree of visual loss as a field of 10 degrees or less in the better eye, or an acuity worse than 6/60 in both eyes?
      `I have a brachial plexus injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a brachial plexus injury (an injury to the nerves running from the neck to the arm)?
      `it has caused the loss of the use of a limb` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: has it resulted in the loss of the use of a limb?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my injury a severe injury` `my injury is` `the percentage of my body burned` `my burns cause severe disfigurement` `I have full-thickness burns to my head, neck, arms or lower legs` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder mobility tasks` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder communication tasks` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder self-care tasks` `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` `my combined visual defects equal that loss` `I have a brachial plexus injury` `it has caused the loss of the use of a limb` MEANS
    `s 3(1), r 5 -- is a severe injury`
        (`my injury` `my injury is` `the percentage of my body burned` `my burns cause severe disfigurement` `I have full-thickness burns to my head, neck, arms or lower legs` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder mobility tasks` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder communication tasks` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder self-care tasks` `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` `my combined visual defects equal that loss` `I have a brachial plexus injury` `it has caused the loss of the use of a limb`)

@export Which part of the definition makes my injury a severe injury (Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) s 3(1)(a), or the Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 5(1)(a), (b) or (c)), if any? The first that applies is given.
GIVEN `my injury is` IS A `Head of s 3(1)(a) other than burns` @desc Is your injury a significant acquired brain injury, paraplegia, quadriplegia or the amputation of a limb? Choose none of these if not.
      `the percentage of my body burned` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of your body was burned (0 if none)?
      `my burns cause severe disfigurement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your burns cause severe disfigurement?
      `I have full-thickness burns to my head, neck, arms or lower legs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your burns include full-thickness burns to your head, neck, arms or lower legs?
      `my full-thickness burns severely hinder mobility tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your full-thickness burns cause severe difficulties in performing mobility tasks?
      `my full-thickness burns severely hinder communication tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your full-thickness burns cause severe difficulties in performing communication tasks?
      `my full-thickness burns severely hinder self-care tasks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your full-thickness burns cause severe difficulties in performing self-care tasks?
      `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many degrees of arc from central fixation is the field of vision of your better eye constricted (enter 90 if your field of vision is not affected)?
      `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the corrected visual acuity of your right eye on the Snellen scale, as a number (6/6 is 1, 6/60 is 0.1, 3/60 is 0.05)?
      `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the corrected visual acuity of your left eye on the Snellen scale, as a number (6/6 is 1, 6/60 is 0.1, 3/60 is 0.05)?
      `my combined visual defects equal that loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been assessed that a combination of your visual defects gives the same degree of visual loss as a field of 10 degrees or less in the better eye, or an acuity worse than 6/60 in both eyes?
      `I have a brachial plexus injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a brachial plexus injury (an injury to the nerves running from the neck to the arm)?
      `it has caused the loss of the use of a limb` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: has it resulted in the loss of the use of a limb?
GIVETH A `Severe injury route`
`Which part of the definition makes my injury a severe injury` `my injury is` `the percentage of my body burned` `my burns cause severe disfigurement` `I have full-thickness burns to my head, neck, arms or lower legs` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder mobility tasks` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder communication tasks` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder self-care tasks` `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` `my combined visual defects equal that loss` `I have a brachial plexus injury` `it has caused the loss of the use of a limb` MEANS
    `s 3(1), r 5 -- the severe injury route`
        (`my injury` `my injury is` `the percentage of my body burned` `my burns cause severe disfigurement` `I have full-thickness burns to my head, neck, arms or lower legs` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder mobility tasks` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder communication tasks` `my full-thickness burns severely hinder self-care tasks` `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` `my combined visual defects equal that loss` `I have a brachial plexus injury` `it has caused the loss of the use of a limb`)

@export Is my loss of sight "permanent blindness" under the Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 5(2)? An injury that results in permanent blindness is a severe injury (r 5(1)(a)).
GIVEN `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many degrees of arc from central fixation is the field of vision of your better eye constricted (enter 90 if your field of vision is not affected)?
      `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the corrected visual acuity of your right eye on the Snellen scale, as a number (6/6 is 1, 6/60 is 0.1, 3/60 is 0.05)?
      `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the corrected visual acuity of your left eye on the Snellen scale, as a number (6/6 is 1, 6/60 is 0.1, 3/60 is 0.05)?
      `my combined visual defects equal that loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been assessed that a combination of your visual defects gives the same degree of visual loss as a field of 10 degrees or less in the better eye, or an acuity worse than 6/60 in both eyes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my loss of sight permanent blindness` `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` `my combined visual defects equal that loss` MEANS
    `r 5(2) -- is permanent blindness` `the field of vision of my better eye in degrees` `the corrected visual acuity of my right eye` `the corrected visual acuity of my left eye` `my combined visual defects equal that loss`

§§ `If my home or vehicle needs modifying (Act s 60(3)-(5); r 11)`

-- Situation: the person reasonably requires a home or vehicle to be modified because of the injury.

@export What is the most the Transport Accident Commission can pay or contribute, in one payment, for modifying my home (or a portable unit or relocation) or my vehicle, without my entering into an agreement with it about ownership and maintenance (Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) s 60(5); Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 11)? $50 000 for a home, $10 000 for a vehicle; unknown outside 23 October 2018 to 5 June 2027.
GIVEN `the payment is for` IS A `Modification payment` @desc Is the payment for modifying your home (or a semi-detachable portable unit, or relocating you) under s 60(4), or for modifying or buying a motor vehicle under s 60(3)?
      `the day of the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or was) the payment to be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most the Commission can pay for my modification without an agreement` `the payment is for` `the day of the payment` MEANS
    `s 60(5), r 11 -- the most without an agreement` `the payment is for` `the day of the payment`

@export Must I enter into an agreement with the Transport Accident Commission about the ownership and maintenance of the modifications before it can make this payment (Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) s 60(5); Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 11)? Yes if the payment exceeds $50 000 for a home or $10 000 for a vehicle.
GIVEN `the payment is for` IS A `Modification payment` @desc Is the payment for modifying your home (or a semi-detachable portable unit, or relocating you) under s 60(4), or for modifying or buying a motor vehicle under s 60(3)?
      `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the payment or contribution, in dollars?
      `the day of the payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day is (or was) the payment to be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I enter into an agreement before the Commission pays for my modification` `the payment is for` `the amount of the payment` `the day of the payment` MEANS
    `s 60(5), r 11 -- an agreement is needed for the payment` `the payment is for` `the amount of the payment` `the day of the payment`

§§ `The forms I must use (rr 6-9, Schedule 1)`

@export Which prescribed form must I use (Transport Accident Regulations 2017 rr 7-9, Schedule 1)? A statement of earnings is Form 1; a driver's or recreation vehicle report on the Commission's notice is Form 2; a train or tram operator's report is Form 3; a trailer contract of insurance is Form 4. Form 1 asks for your name, address and claim number, the statement period, earnings as an employee (dates, employer, weekly hours, gross pay), other earnings (dates, activity, gross earnings), and a signed declaration.
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document is it: a statement of earnings (you receive weekly payments for loss of earning capacity), a report the Commission asked a driver for, a report for a recreation vehicle, a train or tram operator's report, or a trailer contract of insurance?
GIVETH A `Prescribed form`
`Which form must I use` `the document` MEANS
    `rr 7-9 -- the prescribed form` `the document`

§§ `If I receive weekly payments for loss of earning capacity (Act ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5); r 7)`

@export I receive weekly payments for loss of earning capacity: by what day must I give the Transport Accident Commission my statement of earnings in Form 1 after an anniversary of my first payment (Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5); Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 7)? Two months after the anniversary.
GIVEN `the day of my first payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first receive a weekly payment under this section for this accident?
      `which anniversary` IS A NUMBER @desc Which anniversary of that first payment is it (1 for the first, 2 for the second, and so on)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I give my statement of earnings` `the day of my first payment` `which anniversary` MEANS
    `ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) -- the last day for the statement of earnings` `the day of my first payment` `which anniversary`

@export Is my statement of earnings given within the two months after the anniversary of my first weekly payment (Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5); Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 7)? Late, the next review stops weekly payments until it is given (s 55(3)).
GIVEN `the day of my first payment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first receive a weekly payment under this section for this accident?
      `which anniversary` IS A NUMBER @desc Which anniversary of that first payment is it (1 for the first, 2 for the second, and so on)?
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you (or will you) give the statement of earnings to the Commission?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my statement of earnings given in time` `the day of my first payment` `which anniversary` `the day I gave it` MEANS
    `ss 49(4), 50(4), 51(5) -- the statement is given within the two months` `the day of my first payment` `which anniversary` `the day I gave it`

§§ `If the Commission asks me to report an accident (Act s 64; r 8)`

-- Situation: the Commission has served a notice asking for a report of a transport accident.

@export Am I the person who must make the report in Form 2 if the Transport Accident Commission serves a notice asking for one (Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) s 64(1), (3); Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 8(1))? For a motor vehicle, the driver; for a recreation vehicle, the driver if 15 or over, otherwise the owner, or the owner's parent or guardian if the owner was under 15. Not reporting does not affect your right to compensation (s 64(4)).
GIVEN `it was a recreation vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vehicle a recreation vehicle (registered as one under the Road Safety Act 1986)?
      `someone was or may have been injured or killed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was someone injured, or may have been injured, or killed in the accident, so that a person may be entitled to compensation under the Transport Accident Act?
      `I am` IS A `Reporter` @desc Are you the driver, the owner, or the parent or guardian of the owner?
      `the driver's age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old was the driver at the time of the accident?
      `the owner's age` IS A NUMBER @desc How old was the owner at the time of the accident (enter 99 if the owner is not a person, such as a company)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I the one who must report the accident if the Commission asks` `it was a recreation vehicle` `someone was or may have been injured or killed` `I am` `the driver's age` `the owner's age` MEANS
    `s 64(1), (3) -- I am the one who must report on a notice` `it was a recreation vehicle` `someone was or may have been injured or killed` `I am` `the driver's age` `the owner's age`

@export The Transport Accident Commission served me a notice asking for a report of the accident: by what day must I make it in Form 2 (Transport Accident Act 1986 (Vic) s 64(1), (3); Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 8(1))? 28 days after receiving the notice; otherwise a $50 penalty is payable (s 65(2)).
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the Commission's notice?
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I make my accident report` `the day I received the notice` MEANS
    `s 64(1), (3) -- the last day for the report` `the day I received the notice`

§§ `If I own or am in charge of a trailer insured with the Commission (Act s 86; rr 9, 10; Form 4)`

-- Situation: the trailer's owner has a contract of insurance with the Commission under s 86.

@export Is my trailer's contract of insurance with the Transport Accident Commission in (or taken to be in) the prescribed form (Transport Accident Regulations 2017 r 9, Form 4, and the transitional r 10)?
GIVEN `my contract is in Form 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in Form 4 of the Transport Accident Regulations 2017?
      `it complied with the 2007 form before 6 June 2017` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the contract comply (or was it taken to comply) with the form prescribed by regulation 10 of the Transport Accident Regulations 2007 immediately before 6 June 2017?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my trailer insurance contract in the prescribed form` `my contract is in Form 4` `it complied with the 2007 form before 6 June 2017` MEANS
    `r 9, r 10 -- the contract complies with the prescribed form` `my contract is in Form 4` `it complied with the 2007 form before 6 June 2017`

@export Does the trailer contract of insurance (Transport Accident Regulations 2017 Form 4, clauses 2 and 3(1)) indemnify me against this liability? No answer if you are neither the owner nor a person in charge of the trailer, or the liability is not for a death or injury from the trailer's use in Australia.
GIVEN `I am the owner or in charge of the trailer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the trailer's owner named in the Schedule, or a person in charge of the trailer at the time (with or without the owner's authority)?
      `the liability is for death or injury from its use in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability in respect of the death of, or injury to, a person, caused by or arising out of the use of the trailer in Australia?
      `it arose in the period of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it arise during the period of insurance in the Schedule, or a later period for which the Commission accepted a renewal premium?
      `it is a workers' compensation liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a liability to pay compensation under the Accident Compensation Act 1985, or another Act or law referred to in s 37 of the Transport Accident Act 1986 (the workers' compensation and like schemes)?
      `it arises only under another agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the liability arise under an agreement (other than this contract), and would it not have arisen without that agreement?
      `the trailer was registered under the Interstate Road Transport Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time, was the trailer registered in Victoria under the Interstate Road Transport Act 1985 of the Commonwealth (the words of clause 3(1)(c))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my trailer insurance cover me for this liability` `I am the owner or in charge of the trailer` `the liability is for death or injury from its use in Australia` `it arose in the period of insurance` `it is a workers' compensation liability` `it arises only under another agreement` `the trailer was registered under the Interstate Road Transport Act` MEANS
    `Form 4 cl 2, 3(1) -- the contract indemnifies against the liability`
        (`Trailer liability` WITH
            `I am the owner or a person in charge of the trailer`          IS `I am the owner or in charge of the trailer`
            `the liability is for death or injury from the trailer's use in Australia` IS `the liability is for death or injury from its use in Australia`
            `it arose in the period of insurance or an accepted renewal`  IS `it arose in the period of insurance`
            `it is a liability to pay workers' compensation`              IS `it is a workers' compensation liability`
            `it arises only under another agreement`                      IS `it arises only under another agreement`
            `the trailer was registered under the Interstate Road Transport Act 1985` IS `the trailer was registered under the Interstate Road Transport Act`)

@export What is the most the Transport Accident Commission is liable for under my trailer contract of insurance, where another insurance contract also covers the owner (Transport Accident Regulations 2017 Form 4, clause 3(2))? Its rateable proportion of the liability.
GIVEN `the amount of the liability` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the liability covered by the contract, in dollars?
      `another contract covers the owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the event, was there another contract of insurance or indemnity covering the owner for the same liability?
      `the Commission's rateable proportion` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what is the Commission's rateable proportion, as a fraction (for example 0.5 for half)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most the Commission is liable for under my trailer insurance` `the amount of the liability` `another contract covers the owner` `the Commission's rateable proportion` MEANS
    `Form 4 cl 3(2) -- the most the Commission is liable for` `the amount of the liability` `another contract covers the owner` `the Commission's rateable proportion`
